Fri Oct 23 11:03:18 UTC 2026 - Johannes Kastl <opensuse_buildservice@ojkastl.de>

- Update to version 1.35.0:
  * Notable Changes
    - A new --pager flag to pipe output into a pager
      You can now pipe stern's output into a pager with the --pager
      flag. Unlike piping in the shell (stern --color=always
      backend | less -R), colors are preserved without any extra
      flags, and stern stops tailing when you quit the pager.

        stern --pager less backend

      The pager is used only when the standard output is connected
      to a terminal (tty). If you always want to use a pager, set
      it in the config file:

        pager: less

    - Distinct colors for pods created by the same workload
      Pods created by the same workload (e.g. replicas of a
      Deployment) are now assigned distinct colors as long as
      unused colors remain, so that their interleaved logs are
      easier to tell apart. Pods that do not share a workload with
      other pods keep the same colors as before.
    - Nested field extraction in extractJSONParts
      extractJSONParts and tryExtractJSONParts now accept keys in
      dot notation to access nested fields.

        stern --template='{{ extractJSONParts .Message "python.levelname" "message" }}{{"\n"}}' backend

    - The timestamp and the namespace in extjson and ppextjson
      The extjson and ppextjson outputs now include the timestamp
      field when --timestamps is specified, and the namespace field
      when tailing multiple namespaces with --namespace. Nested
      JSON messages in ppextjson are now indented as well.

        $ stern --timestamps -o extjson backend
        {"pod":"backend-...","container":"backend","timestamp":"2026-10-01T10:00:00.123456789Z","message":"hello"}

  * Breaking Changes
    - .Message no longer includes the timestamp with --timestamps
      With --timestamps, the timestamp is no longer prepended to
      .Message in templates, so template functions that parse
      .Message as JSON now work with --timestamps. The timestamp is
      available as the new .Timestamp template variable. The output
      of the built-in default and raw templates is unchanged, but
      if you use a custom template with --timestamps, add
      .Timestamp to it to keep printing the timestamp.

        stern --timestamps --template='{{.Timestamp}} {{.Message}}{{"\n"}}' backend

  * Changes
    - fix: close config file after reading (#367) ee5b0b3
    - fix: change errorf format to represent real value (#368)
      0d39b3f
    - docs: fix "when if" typo in max-log-requests table (#371)
      13b9806
    - Keep .Message raw with --timestamps; expose timestamp as
      .Timestamp (#372) 8a00e61
    - Support nested field extraction via dot notation in
      extractJSONParts (#373) 3dd605b
    - docs: list toUTC in README template functions (#378) 2926461
    - Fix misspelled identifiers reHightlight and stirngSlice
      (#382) 523c01a
    - fix: honor --timestamps when reading from stdin (#380)
      96b3c3a
    - fix: include the namespace in extjson and ppextjson for
      multiple namespaces (#386) d6d42c9
    - fix: preserve the sign of fractional Unix timestamps (#388)
      6db257e
    - docs: fix the function name in the colorCustom example (#383)
      050c9fe
    - Assign distinct colors to pods created by the same workload
      (#375) 74000c2
    - Add --pager flag to pipe output into a pager (#376) 4772306
    - Hide the namespace when --namespace repeats a single
      namespace (#389) b4b5d59
    - Update dependencies for Kubernetes 1.37 (#390) e62aec2
    - fix: show the timestamp in extjson and ppextjson output
      (#392) 5e330c6
    - Marshal extjson and ppextjson outputs with encoding/json
      instead of string concatenation (#393) 7ef2365
    - fix: keep inline regexp flags within their own --highlight
      pattern (#395) 9a830a0

